cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, cite this software and the relevant original mathematical sources."
title: "HeavyTailedNoise: Lean 4 formalization of stochastic optimization bounds"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Xiong"
    given-names: "Zhixiao"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xiong-zx/heavy-tailed-noise-lean"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of the complete finite-q lower bound for arbitrary
  randomized strict-K=1 algorithms, including the Bernoulli-chain baseline
  and gated Haar term,
  for stochastic optimization with bounded p-th central moments and
  global same-seed q-increment bounds, and the first-slot-normalized
  Fradin v2 Theorem 3.1 on the original response-only zero-respecting
  shared-seed batch protocol. The library also contains reusable model,
  analysis, probability, and upper-bound foundations. The integrated
  218-module canonical native build, full provenance audit, 18-entry
  public signature and axiom audit, and standalone full-entry import
  check passed locally on 27 September 2026. The complete lower bound
  retains an absolute relative accuracy condition and fixed natural
  response budgets; no complete upper-rate or infinite-q theorem is claimed.
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "stochastic optimization"
  - "heavy-tailed noise"
  - "complexity lower bounds"
  - "formal verification"
